anding proudly  amidst ruins a forest blanketed in an  ominous fog it was all overwhelming and  none of the hardships i'd experienced in  demon souls dark souls bloodborne or  sakura have come close to making me feel  as small at the same time i was overcome  with excitement for what the lands  between had in store for me and all the  seemingly insurmountable battles  awaiting and it did not disappoint elden  ring is from software's crowning  achievement in world design epic in  scale and scope but what makes it  special isn't just how visually stunning  it all is or that its open world is vast  rich in detail and teeming with  possibilities instead it's how the  studio has applied its own esoteric  design principles to deliver an  experience that feels fresh elegant and  uniquely from software the game's core  pillars are built on the same strong  action and role-playing foundations as  previous titles while offering more  freedom to explore than ever before  eldon ring is an open world game  entirely in a category of its own that  delicate orchestration of highs and lows  and the build up and release of tension  that from software has mastered coupled  with the thrill of free form exploration  and discovery is an intoxicating  cocktail of game design a key part of  from software's design ethos is to strip  down to the essentials and in elden ring  that process strengthens exploration and  discovery the heart and soul of the  experience the studios games typically  give the player very little while asking  a lot an elden ring is the most obtuse  and demanding of his game so far this is  largely because everything you've come  to expect from modern day open world  games is absent for instance there's no  map until you find an item that reveals  the topography of a region even then the  points of interest in that region aren't  marked until you've been there and seen  them there is no mini-map just a compass  that shows the cardinal directions and  any waypoints you've placed areas you go  to won't be gated depending on your  level there's no clear indication on  when you should go to key locations the  best you get is at the sites of grace  which function as rest points in the  same way that bonfires lanterns or idols  did in other titles at each of these  sites is a dim trail of golden light  pointing in the general direction of  something perhaps it's the next  milestone on your quest or maybe it's  just another area that has a dungeon the  only way to find out is to make the  journey the challenge for from software  lies in the friction between the  studio's design hallmarks and the  expected conventions of a genre filled  with games that try to be all things to  everyone and although the execution is  an unmitigated success one thing's for  sure eldon ring is not a smooth edged  one-size-fits-all kind of experience  that will accommodate everyone instead  it's unrelentingly opaque relishes in  the savagery of confronting players with  unfavorable odds and delights in  watching the ensuing struggle elden  ring's gameplay will feel familiar to  those with experience of previous from  software games the tried and true  formula of measured third person combat  against enemies that are swift to punish  full holiness is both as thrilling and  as nerve-wracking as ever from software  has added some new gameplay wrinkles to  its soul's bone formula this time most  notable is a jump which has been pulled  out from the more dynamic movement style  of sakura this is useful not just for  traversal but also for performing a  leaping strike that can break through an  enemy's defense and create a critical  strike opportunity another new mechanic  is the ability to strike back after  blocking an enemy's attack with a heavy  counter dealing a good amount of damage  the heavy counter has some of the  satisfaction of bloodborne's gunshot and  visceral combo though it's not as  gratifyingly dramatic while it's easy to  rely on it a great deal